quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  2,265,"And the example of those who spend their wealth seeking Allah’s pleasure and reassuring themselves (in their belief) is that of a garden on a hill-side—if heavy rain falls upon it, it yields up its fruits twofold; even if no rain falls upon it, (it is watered by) the dew. Allah is All-Seeing of what you do."
  2,266,"Would anyone of you like to have a garden of palm trees and grapevines with streams flowing beneath it, with all kinds of fruit for him therein, and old age overtakes him while he has weak offspring, then a fiery hurricane strikes it and burns it down? In this way, Allah clarifies His communications for you so that you may reflect."
  2,267,"O believers! Spend from the good things you have earned (lawfully) and from what We have produced for you from the earth, and do not intend to give the bad part of it as charity, which you would not accept for yourselves unless you overlook it. And know that Allah is All-Sufficient, All-Praiseworthy."
  2,268,"Satan threatens you with poverty and prompts you to indecency, whereas Allah promises you (His) pardon and bounty. And Allah is All-Embracing, All-Knowing."
  2,269,"He grants wisdom to whom He pleases, and whoever is granted wisdom is certainly given an abundant good. Yet none will remember except those possessing insight."
